 "question": "Compare the three meanings of 'index' in data wrangling.",
 "answer": "The term 'index' in data wrangling refers to three distinct concepts: a database index, a pandas Index, and a Python list index. [S1] A database index in [S1] is a data structure that enhances lookup speed but slows down writes and requires additional storage. A pandas Index [S1] is the row labels of a DataFrame, maintaining the structure of the data. A Python list index [S1] is an integer position starting at 0, referring to elements in a list. These are unrelated [S1].",
